From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1048 redfin: kern.sweet_surf_inuse: every IOSurface publishes
 its use count (with GPU holds) where IOSurfaceIsInUse reads it

0983 wrote state page +0x18 only for scanout-slot surfaces, so every other
surface (CVPixelBufferPool camera buffers, Photos/ImageIO decode surfaces,
CA's caches) always read "not in use" and pools recycled it while
backboardd's GPU work still sampled it: mixed pictures in Photos
thumbnails, camera preview jumping back in time.

IOSurfaceIsInUse (iOS 16.7 IOSurface.framework, recon/mg/iosurf2.bin
+0x4d0) is ldr x8,[x0,#0x70] (the client's state page); ldr x8,[x8,#0x18];
cmp x8,#0; cset: the u64 at +0x18 != 0, as hackios MiniIOSurface's
minisurf_shared.useCount (category 1 << 32 | category 0).

kern.sweet_surf_inuse (boot-arg sweetsurfinuse sets the start value):
0 (default) = 0983 exactly. 1 = every surface publishes clientUse +
displayUse + gpuHold (category 0) and clientUse1; a client's own use
counts are dropped with its reference (exit/crash). gpuHold: the v2 ABI's
submits carry only IBs, so each v2 submit holds every IOSurface its client
has imported and GPU-mapped (import matched to a surface by the physical
address of its first byte, once per import) until the submit's fence
lands; a kernel thread woken by the GPU interrupt (5 ms poll fallback,
2 s cap) drops the holds. 2 = 1 + 5 s klog line "SWEET SURF INUSE: 5s:
...". 3 = 2 without GPU holds (to tell the two effects apart).
Switching 1 -> 0 clears the non-slot surfaces' published counts.
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c                   |  24 ++
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAccelerator.cpp |  47 ++++
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp     | 353 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.h       |  16 ++
 4 files changed, 435 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

